 "about": "How figures are said (ED1a, editing design section 3C). For each kind of quantity and what it is about, the readings a click steps through (first is the default), each a ladder of rungs. Every unit is a row of the master data sheet's Units table (packs/base-reference): no factor is typed here. `fact_about` says what a card's fact is about from its field (a_au is an orbit, radius_earth a size), so it reads like the same value anywhere else; a world's surface temperature reads in °C first, like a site's. A rung whose unit the sheet does not hold yet is skipped. 'from' is where a rung takes over, in that rung's own unit. Words (thousand, million) are written above plain_below; exponents when nothing fits. This table moves into a pack with unit schemes (MP15).",
